\ Test quotation-level stack effect validation

\ A quotation with a leading stack effect gets that effect attached
\ and validated when executed

\ Correct effect: ( n -- n ) preserves one value
1 [ ( n -- n ) dup drop ] call
.
5 [ ( n -- n ) dup drop ] call
.

\ Incorrect effect should fail but be catchable with recover
\ recover-quot has declared effect ( error -- ) so we must only consume the error
5 [ ( n -- n ) dup ] [ drop "caught" . ] recover

\ Effect ( -- ) means no inputs, no outputs
[ ( -- ) ] call
.

\ Effect ( -- n ) means produces one value
[ ( -- n ) 42 ] call
.

\ Nested quotations each have their own effect validation
10 [ ( n -- n n ) dup ] call
.
.
